  <completion date="2026-10-29">
    Delivered (PR #2418, merged to docs `7cb3c263c0`, final head `1eef127052`): Assign Task's "Send email notification" emails the assignee and, for an internal user, raises the bell (D-194). The owner's D-199 decides who receives it, through one gate (`AssignTaskRecipientGate`) on every send path: the in-request send, the system-mailbox fallback, and the job's send-time recheck.
    - An eligible internal user: exactly one enabled user represents the contact; the No Access check (AsFlagged) is NotSecure or NotWalled; the user has Read on the task.
    - An onboarded external contact: needs a grant with Read on the matter, the task must be one the portal's events list would show (the multi-root / secure-family rule, `CheckLiveParentsAsync`), and access is composed the way the contact's portal sign-in does it (CIAM, or WorkforceHome with derived-member terms). A home-linked licensed user gets no email. They get the portal link and the assigner's display name, and no bell.
    - Nobody else, and nobody when the check can't be made (fail closed). The task is still created, and the wizard says why no email went.
    Fixed from the reviews:
    - the record name only through `InquiryRecordFacts`; the tracked email internal-only (read back);
    - real DI-wiring tests; "Assigned by" plus `sprk_sentby`;
    - Poisoned on a permanent 4xx, but 408/429 retry;
    - Restricted fails closed on tables without flags; direct seam tests;
    - the job uses the task's current filing.
    The CIAM and workforce principal compositions are lifted into internal statics; R3 approved them as behaviour-preserving.
    Known limits:
    - K1: Graph can send twice after a timeout (no idempotency key).
    - K3: the commit request is slower (D-194 sends in-request).
    - K4: an old client shows a stray text box until it reloads.
    - A row edited by hand outside the BFF.
    Reviews: the first Opus adversarial review (2 F1, F3, K2s); a second Opus pass on fix round 1 (2 F1, F3, K2); uac-r2 on every round (the multi-root F, the stored home pair); R3 on the resolver lifts (the workforce-plane under-notify) and approved them. The main session re-checked each fix diff.
    Final numbers: AssignTask 145/145, the wider filters green, ArchTests 1665/1665, every guard mutation-checked (18, then 15, 7 and 2 per round), publish delta +5.6 KB zipped in round 3 (+25.6 KB in round 2; 192 files).
    Filed: DI-135 #2445 (the portal shows tasks as generic events; R4), DI-136 #2457 (swap in ContactUserRepresentation when uac-r2 193 merges), DI-137 #2458 (the GrantAccessNotifier home-link gap; external access).
    Open: the owner question on the From address for external assignees (A: always the system mailbox; B: as built). The live dev proof (email + bell, and the external portal view) waits for the next dev BFF deploy (UAC's 194b hold).
    rework: fix-round-4 task 168
  </completion>
</task>
